li><span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">Rate of pay: €15.40 per hour</span>, and you will be paid for the number of hours of your working shift.</li><li>Payment will be processed <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">within two weeks</span> after the event.</li><li>Your <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">IBAN must be Irish</span> (such as AIB, BOI, PTSB, Revolut IE).</li><li>Ensure your bank details are correct to avoid delays.<br></li></ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 600;\">App requirements<br></span></p><ul><li>Register your <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">bank details</span> and <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">PPS number</span> in the <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">Profile</span> section of the app.</li><li>This is an <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">availability enquiry only, </span>applying for an event does not confirm your spot.</li><li>After submitting your application, keep an eye on your <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">status</span>. If selected, it will update to “<span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">Confirmed”</span>.</li></ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 600;\">What to wear</span></p><ul><li>Black top/jumper, black trousers and black shoes preferred. Choose <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">comfortable</span> clothing.</li></ul><p><span style=\"font-weight: 600;\">Food &amp; break<br></span></p><h4></h4><p><span style=\"font-weight: 600;\"></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">You’re entitled to a break</span>, scheduled by the bar supervisor. You may use it to rest, eat, drink water or simply recharge before returning to your position.</li><li>Bring your <span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">pre-packed food</span>, or you can buy food at the event.</li><li>Please, bring your <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\">water bottle.</span> There will be taps with drinking water available for refilling. Let\'s avoid using disposable plastic, <span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\">help save the planet! :)<br></span></li></ul><p><span data-token-index=\"0\" class=\"notion-enable-hover\" style=\"font-weight: 600;\">Attendance &amp; Conduct</span><font color=\"#333b3f\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"></span></font></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\">No-show without justification</span>, or&nbsp; cancellation on the event day, may affect your participation in future events :(</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(141, 148, 152); font-weight: 400;\">Maintain </span>professional communication</span>, follow instructions from supervisors, and stay in your assigned area unless told otherwise.</li></ul>', 'https://chat.whatsapp.com/CsozfEP7FAZDXW2O1ROzzr', 0, 1, 1, 1, '2026-07-10 13:53:06', '2026-07-20 00:00:04'),
(23, 'Lidl Event', 'Captura-de-tela-2026-07-15-141034.png', NULL, '2026-07-25', '2026-07-25', NULL, NULL, 'Lidl RDC Newbridge, Littleconnell, Newbridge, County Kildare, Irlanda', '53.1909047', '-6.7693846', NULL, 'Littleconnell, County Kildare, W12 KT98, Irlanda', '53.19184569999999', '-6.7685974', 'Final confirmation will be provided later.', 'General duties', 4, 1, 15.40, 'Lidl: Family-Friendly Farm Experience (Newbridge)', '<ul><li>The event is outside Dublin.<br><br></li><li><span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: rgb(51, 59, 63);\">€15.40/hour</span> (this is a registered job).<br><br></li><li><strong>9:00 AM – 4:00 PM (TBC)</strong>  \r\nWe will confirm the final time and dress code by the end of the week.</li></ul>', '<p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">You will support the event with general duties, including:</span></p><ul role=\"list\"><li><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Greeting guests</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Working at reception</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Directing parking</span></p></li><li><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Assisting with guest flow and outdoor activities</span></p></li></ul>', '<p>This is a family-friendly farm experience event for adults and children.</p><p>Guests will enjoy outdoor activities, entertainment, and food options.</p>', 'https://chat.whatsapp.com/J7qwqJX6MMg2TIcUHdeDyY', 0, 1, 1, 1, '2026-07-15 14:13:00', '2026-07-26 00:00:04'),
(24, 'Electric Picnic', '2429006s.jpg', NULL, '2026-08-28', '2026-08-31', NULL, NULL, 'Stradbally Hall, Stradbally, Co. Laois, Ireland', '53.0106018', '-7.155545999999999', NULL, 'Vicar Street, Thomas Street, The Liberties, Dublin 8, Irlanda', '53.34267639999999', '-6.2778366', 'Times to be confirmed. \r\n• Meeting time: 6:30am (bus leaves Dublin on Friday 7:00AM from Vicar Street. 58-59, Thomas St, The Liberties, Dublin 8). \r\n\r\n\r\n• Bus returns to Dublin (Vicar St) to the same meeting point on Sunday night/early Monday\r\n• There’s a chance the bus might only return on Monday morning, so this information is TBC.', 'Bar Staff', 50, 1, 15.40, 'Ireland’s largest gathering of music & arts, and the ultimate rock n’ roll circus, Electric Picnic has established itself as one of the world’s most unique festivals. With a great selection of music, art, theatre, comedy, food and holistic health, it’s the most delightfully diverse end of summer party on the Emerald Isle.', '<p><font color=\"#333b3f\"><strong>Availability &amp; Camping</strong></font></p><p><font color=\"#333b3f\"><strong><br></strong></font></p><p>• You must be <strong>available for all 3 days</strong> of the festival (there\'s no bus leaving Dublin on Saturday)</p><p>• We’ll be <strong>camping on-site</strong> for the weekend. You have to bring your own tent, mattress and sleeping bag</p><p>• You have to bring your own food</p><p>• Shower facilities will be available in the staff camping area</p><p>• This is a registered job</p><p>• <strong>This is a client event, not organized by us</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>What to wear</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• Black top/jumper, black trousers and black shoes preferred. Choose comfortable clothing.</p><p>• You\'ll be given a branded t-shirt on the day.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Important</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• Your application will only be confirmed once you join in the WhatsApp group.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">• This is a client event and is not organized by us. Our role is to provide staff, so decisions regarding shifts, on-site management, and the overall organization of the event are outside of our control.</p><p>That said, we are committed to making the experience as positive as possible for everyone involved. We will always do our best to provide support and assist wherever we can, within the scope of our role and responsibilities.</p>', '<p>\r\n<!-- notionvc: 2c7d702b-94ad-4722-a048-0661143534b0 --></p><p>We will all be working as part of the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\">bar team.</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(51, 59, 63); font-weight: 700;\"></span>During the event, staff can be assigned to different bar positions, each supporting the service and helping the team run smoothly:</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>Tills:</strong> Operating the cash register, taking orders, charging customers, and keeping the queue moving smoothly</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>Server:</strong> Serving drinks to customers, keeping the area tidy, and helping with whatever is needed</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>Pouring:</strong> Pouring pints on the tap, ensuring good quality and serving efficiently</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>N/P:</strong> Managing the serving of canned spirits, keeping stock organised, and ensuring fast service</p><p>•&nbsp;<strong>Runners:</strong> Restocking cups, drinks, supporting the bar team, and ensuring nothing runs out</p>', '<p><strong>Shift information</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• Your shift position will be informed<strong> before the event</strong>.</p><p>• Your shift time will be displayed <strong>at the top of this page or it can be informed through the WhatsAppGroup</strong></p><p>• Follow all instructions from the bar manager and supervisors.</p><p>• Stay in your assigned position unless instructed otherwise.</p><p>• Keep communication clear and check the group for updates throughout the day.</p><p>• And most importantly, <strong>have fun</strong>! :D</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Clock-in &amp; Clock-out</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• You must<strong> clock in and clock out at the exact time</strong> of your assigned shift.</p><p>• Any overtime must be approved by the bar manager and recorded in the notes field.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Payment information</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• Rate of pay: <strong>€15.40 per hour</strong>, and you will be paid for the number of hours of your working shift.</p><p>• Payment will be processed within two weeks after the event.</p><p>• <strong>Your IBAN must be Irish </strong>(such as AIB, BOI, PTSB, Revolut IE).</p><p>• Ensure your bank details are correct to avoid delays.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>App requirements</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>• Register your bank details and PPS number in the Profile section of the app.</p><p>• This is an availability enquiry only, applying for an event does not confirm your spot.</p><p>• After submitting your application, keep an eye on your status. If selected, it will update to “<strong>Confirmed</strong>”.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Food &amp; break</strong></p><p>• You’re entitled to a break, scheduled by the bar supervisor. You may use it to rest, eat, drink water or simply recharge before returning to your position.</p><p>• Bring your pre-packed food, or you can buy food at the event.</p><p>• Please, bring your water bottle. There will be taps with drinking water available for refilling. Let\'s avoid using disposable plastic, help save the planet! :)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attendance &amp; Conduct</strong></p><p>•<strong> No-show without justification, or cancellation on the event day, may affect your participation in future events :(</strong></p><p>• Maintain professional communication, follow instructions from supervisors, and stay in your assigned area unless told otherwise.</p>', 'https://chat.whatsapp.com/LYadHKjDzJ1Gs2juzMyuJl', 0, 1, 0, 1, '2026-08-06 16:43:14', '2026-08-28 00:00:05'),
(25, 'Hospitality Shift', 'Captura-de-tela-2026-08-11-131451.png', NULL, '2026-08-21', '2026-08-21', NULL, NULL, 'Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, Fonthill Road, Clondalkin, Dublin, Irlanda', '53.3526192', '-6.3930247', NULL, 'Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, Fonthill Road, Clondalkin, Dublin, Irlanda', '53.3526192', '-6.3930247', 'TBC', 'Hospitality', 2, 0, 15.40, 'General hospitality support during promotional activity at Liffey Valley Shopping Centre.', '<p>-</p>', '<p>Engaging with customers, handing out merchandise, showing people menu for new restaurant, que management.&nbsp;</p>', '<p></p><div></div><p></p><p><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Staff must send a headshot along with 3 to 4 previous jobs and 3 to 4 roles they have carried out for client review.</span></p>', '.', 0, 1, 1, 1, '2026-08-11 13:17:38', '2026-08-22 00:00:04'),
(28, 'Load in & out', 'Captura-de-tela-2026-08-27-145053.png', NULL, '2026-09-07', '2026-09-15', NULL, NULL, 'Dalymount Park, Dalymount, Phibsborough, Dublin, Irlanda', '53.3618671', '-6.274961299999999', NULL, 'Dalymount Park, Dalymount, Phibsborough, Dublin, Irlanda', '53.3618671', '-6.274961299999999', '-', 'Crew', 10, 0, 15.40, 'Event crew support for load in and load.\r\n\r\nAccess the link to confirm the selected crew names for each day: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/13dj78Mvp_WhBlt8_0qPD1V4MzJPyr6ZlA-xm37PhzcM/edit?usp=sharing', '<p><strong>Arrival at 08h00.</strong></p><p>Note: some shifts are TBC and may change.</p><p><br></p>', '<p>-</p>', '<p>-</p>', '-', 0, 0, 0, 1, '2026-08-27 15:10:49', '2026-08-27 16:09:26');
