(882, 496, 16, '2026-07-31', '2026-08-01', '12:00:00', '02:40:00', '2026-07-31 12:00:00', '2026-08-01 02:40:00', NULL, 'Hi! I didn\'t notice the WhatsApp message saying that I should check my shift on the spreadsheet. Instead, I checked the schedule on the website, which showed my shift as 11:00 to 22:30. Because of that, I ended up starting at 12:00.  I\'m leaving now at 2:40. The bar was very busy, and I forgot to clock out at 1:30. I wasn\'t able to clock out at the correct time, which should have been 1:30.  It\'s completely my mistake for not checking the spreadsheet. I don\'t mind if my shift is recorded as finishing at 1:30, even though I stayed until 2:40. There\'s no need to count the extra time as overtime—it\'s absolutely fine to record my normal shift only.', 1, '2026-07-31 11:00:21', '2026-08-02 12:24:29'),
